  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to look toward; to pay attention to",
      "explanation": "To turn one's gaze toward something, or to show interest in something. Most commonly used in the negative form {見向|みむ}きもしない (to not even glance at, to completely ignore)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "16687_mimuku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{誰|だれ}も{見向|みむ}きもしなかった。",
      "english": "Nobody even looked.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "16687_mimuku_ex2",
      "japanese": "あの{店|みせ}は{客|きゃく}に{見向|みむ}きもされない。",
      "english": "That shop is completely ignored by customers.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "16687_mimuku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{安|やす}い{商品|しょうひん}には{見向|みむ}きもせず、{高級品|こうきゅうひん}ばかり{買|か}う。",
      "english": "Without even glancing at cheap products, they only buy luxury items.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\nAlmost always used in the negative pattern {見向|みむ}きもしない, meaning \"to not pay the slightest attention to\" or \"to completely ignore.\" The affirmative form is rarely used.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {見向|みむ}きもしない (to not even glance at)\n- {見向|みむ}きもされない (to be completely ignored)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {無視|むし}する: to ignore — a more direct and common word for ignoring\n- {振|ふ}り{向|む}く: to turn around — to physically turn to look",
